# cw117, the pocket stones (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw117
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_wald_larkwell
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the pocket stones
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm drive=steady
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk collects_smooth_stones_from_the_riverbanks
likes blackberries dancing full_larder summer_evenings
dislikes night_noise smoke
fears a_home_without_food a_fire_left_unwatched
hopes a_small_farm_of_own a_larder_ready_for_winter
topics home +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.4 food +0.4 dreams +0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carries a #stone# from each riverbank walk, keeps the #still# tended, and pictures a #field# beside a full #larder#.

words
oath! = By bank and bottle | Water on the stones
saying! = The river rounds what it keeps | A full shelf eases the mind
stone = stone | smooth river pebble
stones = stones | rounded pebbles
pocket = pocket | coat pocket
bank = bank | riverbank
river = river | Long River
water = water | clear water
shore = shore | lake shore
lake = lake | Glasswater
reed = reed | bank reed
reeds = reeds | bank reeds
still = still | copper still
copper = copper | red metal
pipe = pipe | cooling pipe
flame = flame | low fire
heat = heat | steady warmth
steam = steam | rising vapour
jar = jar | sealed jar
jars = jars | stoppered jars
cask = cask | wooden cask
smoke = smoke | bitter smoke
window = window | open window
berry = berry | blackberry
berries = berries | blackberries
bush = bush | berry bush
larder = larder | food cupboard
shelf = shelf | kitchen shelf
field = field | small field
farm = farm | little holding
seed = seed | seed grain
soil = soil | dark earth
dance = dance | festival dance
step = step | dance step
evening = evening | long dusk
night = night | dark hours
noise = noise | loud clatter
door = door | home door
home = home | own hearth
coin = coin | pay
bread = bread | loaf
price = price | asking cost
road = road | high path

any
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A full #larder# for one household means little if a neighbour has no #bread#. | I will share a #shelf# before a child goes hungry.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I watch the #price# of #bread# climb while my #coin# stays the same. | A seller should show the measure before taking payment.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A House owns a #field#; I would like to work one of my own. | Their benches are full enough without hearing how a small #farm# might begin.
opinion @1 city against 1 : #smoke.capitalize# and #noise# would make a city hard on me. | A #bank# with moving #water# is enough company for me.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : A new neighbour can join a #dance# without knowing every #step#. | I will show someone the #road# once I know where they mean to go.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I can offer a #berry# and still keep my own counsel. | A quiet stranger may be easier company than a loud friend.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I like a #dance# near the edge of the gathering. | By late #evening# I want the path home.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : The #still# makes work, and a #jar# has its place. | A crowded drinking room soon sends me outside for the river air.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #river# has left me another #stone#. | #greet#. Come in, but leave the #door# quiet.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. We can speak quietly by the #bank#. | #greet#. Speak softly; the #still# needs an ear.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I found #berries# if you would like some. | There is room by the #shelf# for you.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. The #flame# wants watching. | Come nearer the #pipe#; your words will reach me.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #bank# is cool at this hour. | #greet#. I have set the #flame# low for the morning.
line @1 greet.return : Another walk brought you here. | #welcome_back#. The #jar# is sealed now.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept a few #berries# for you. | The #stones# from my last walk are on the #shelf#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come home. I have #bread# on the #shelf#. | The #door# is open for you.
line @1 again.open : You have found me twice today. | I have only gathered one #stone# since we spoke.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep your footing by the #bank#. | #saying.capitalize#. Take the quiet #road#.
line @1 farewell.return : I will save the next smooth #stone# to show you. | May you reach a warm #home#.
line @1 react.news : I will listen. Leave me a moment to lower the #flame#. | Tell it slowly; I do not need the loud version.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not reached me by the #river#. | Who first brought the word to town?
line @1 react.news.known : A fragment came to me along the #shore#. | That gives me the missing part.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would see another account before I pass that along. | The #stones# tell less than they seem; so might this tale.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit here until you are ready. | That is a hard weight to carry home.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A good word. I hope they have a full #shelf# tonight. | I am glad to hear it.
line @1 answer.how : Warm enough, and the #larder# holds. | Steady. I took a walk by the #river#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Watching the #heat# and sealing #jars#. | Busy with the #pipe#, but I can talk.
line @1 ask.how : Has your #home# been quiet? | Did you find supper before the #evening#?
line @1 sympathise : Sit here; I will give you my attention. | You may take your time; the #stone# can wait.
line @1 reassure : One #seed# can make a #field# worth tending. | Let us find one thing that can be done today.
line @1 decline : I must mind the #flame# for now. | That task is beyond what I can promise today.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand. We can leave it there. | Fair enough; another #road# may open.
line @1 thank : That spared me a hard walk. Thank you. | The next heavy task can come to my paws.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was going along the #bank# anyway. | There were #berries# enough to share.
line @1 preclose : The #still# needs its last look. | I want to be home before the #noise# starts.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : That #stone# is smoother than your last #dance# step. | You have taken the finest #berry# again.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #pipe# is sound. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will think on it.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #flame# low before opening the #window#. | Choose #seed# you can plant in the #soil# you have.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : The #road# by the #bank# is lonely now. | Take company if you must travel after dark.
scene river_stones
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take a #stone# from the #bank# when one sits right in my paw. | The #river# has rounded the sharpness off these #stones#.
b : Do you keep every one? | How do you choose?
a : Only the ones I remember finding. | By touch, before I look.

scene pocket_weight
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stone# in my #pocket# reminds me to slow down. | I empty the #pocket# before washing the coat.
b : Does it work? | Have you lost one?
a : More often than a shouted warning. | Once. I found another by the same #bank#.

scene jar_cooling
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A warm #jar# waits on the #shelf# until I can touch it safely. | I leave space between #jars# for the air to move.
b : Does that take long? | What happens if you stack them early?
a : Longer on a still day. | The #heat# stays trapped between them.

scene watching_flame
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #flame# low enough to hear the #pipe#. | Too much #heat# makes the #copper# complain.
b : Can you hear a fault? | Do you ever step away?
a : A change in the sound can tell me. | Only when another hand takes the watch.

scene smoke_at_window
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I open the #window# when #smoke# gathers. | The #still# should smell of work, not a choking #flame#.
b : Does smoke mean trouble? | Does the cold air help?
a : It means I check the fire first. | Enough to clear my head.

scene berries_in_hand
when topic=food here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #berries.capitalize# taste best off the #bush#. | I bring a small handful of #berries# home if the #road# passes the thicket.
b : Do you wash them? | Are there enough to share?
a : If the #bank# has splashed them. | Usually, if I do not eat them all first.

scene larder_count
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full #larder# lets me sleep through an ordinary #night#. | I check the #shelf# before buying more #bread#.
b : Is there enough for winter? | Do you keep a list?
a : Not yet, but we are adding to it. | In my head until the #price# changes.

scene farm_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I picture a small #farm# with a #field# I can cross before supper. | I would plant #seed# close enough to see from the #door#.
b : Would you leave the still? | What would you grow first?
a : If I could make the land pay. | Something that fills a #larder#.

scene first_seeds
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #farm# begins with good #soil#, not a fancy fence. | I would test the #field# after rain before putting in #seed#.
b : Do you know the work? | Could you afford land?
a : Some. I would learn the rest. | Not today. I keep saving #coin#.

scene summer_bank
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long #evening# lets me walk the #bank# after work. | The #stones# hold a little #heat# after the sun leaves.
b : Do you go far? | Do you stay until dark?
a : Until the #river# bends away from the #road#. | I come back before the #noise# of night.

scene quiet_night
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A silent #shore# after dark lets me rest. | A late #noise# carries over the #lake# farther than its maker thinks.
b : Does it wake you? | Do you go see what it is?
a : Often. I listen until it stops. | Only if it sounds like someone needs help.

scene dance_at_edge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I will #dance# if there is space at the edge. | I can follow a #step# without joining the loudest group.
b : Do you know the old dances? | Do you stay late?
a : Enough to find my way through one. | Until the music grows too loud.

scene partner_step
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse# knows when I want a #dance# and when I want the #road# home. | We can miss a #step# and still finish together.
b : Do you practise? | Who leads?
a : Not outside a festival. | Whoever remembers the next turn.

scene child_stones
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I show #self.child# how to feel a #stone# for rough edges. | A child can find a better pebble than I can if I let them choose.
b : Does your child keep them too? | Where do the stones go afterward?
a : Some, until the #pocket# grows heavy. | Set a few on the #shelf# and leave the rest by the #bank#.

scene river_after_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain makes the #river# carry fresh #stones# past the #bank#. | I wait for the #water# to fall before I go looking.
b : Is the bank dangerous then? | Do the stones change?
a : It can be slippery. | The grit washes off and shows their colours.

scene price_of_bread
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #price# of #bread# rises while a day's pay stands still. | I keep an eye on the #larder# before spending spare #coin#.
b : Do you buy less? | Does the still pay enough?
a : I waste less. | Enough for today, not the #farm# I want.

scene reeds_at_lake
when topic=home here.region=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #reeds# by the #lake# move even when the street is still. | I take the #shore# path when the #road# has grown noisy.
b : Do you meet anyone there? | Is it a longer walk?
a : Sometimes a neighbour with the same idea. | A little. I do not mind.

story first_stone [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I found a flat #stone# at the #bank# while I was meant to be hurrying home.
  : I carried it in my #pocket# and kept touching its edge along the #road#.
  ask : Did you keep that first one?
  b : A stone with a story is harder to throw back.
  : I did. It sits on my #shelf# among the others.

story berry_basket [topic=food self.age>=25]
  : I went out for #berries# and came home with more #stones# than fruit.
  : The best #bush# had already been picked, so I walked farther along the #bank#.
  ask : Did you find any berries at all?
  b : Enough for a taste, perhaps.
  : A handful. We ate them before the #larder# door was open.

story low_flame [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I let the #flame# grow too high while I was counting #jars#.
  : The #pipe# changed its sound, so I lowered the fire and watched until it settled.
  ask : Was anything lost?
  b : You caught it early if you heard the pipe.
  : Nothing but time. Since then I listen before I count.

rule @bark_stone
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This #stone# will fit in my #pocket#. | The #river# has polished this one well.

rule @bark_flame
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Keep the #flame# steady. | The #pipe# sounds right for now.

rule @bark_berry
when concept=bark here.season=summer|autumn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There may be #berries# beyond the #bank#. | A ripe #berry# would suit this walk.

rule @bark_night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 9h
say What is making that #noise#? | A quiet #night# would be welcome.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Come nearer if you have something to say. | #greet#. I can listen by the #window#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : We have spoken before. Is all well? | I know you. Come in from the #road#.
dlg @1 resident.job : The #still# needs a careful ear and each #jar# a sound seal. | I keep the #flame# steady while the #still# works.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #bank# is slippery after rain. | #saying.capitalize#. Perhaps our paths will meet along the #river#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you carry stones? -> stones
node stones
say I pick one up on a #river# walk if it feels smooth in my paw. Each recalls the place I found it.
free
choice Do you keep them all? -> shelf
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node shelf
say No. A few stay on the #shelf# at #home#. The rest go back to the #bank#.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
